'faqs'=>[['Can you be depressed without feeling sad?','Yes. Depression may involve loss of interest, numbness, irritability, fatigue, cognitive difficulty or physical symptoms. Assessment considers the complete pattern and its impact.'],['Can someone with depression still work normally?','Yes. Some people maintain responsibilities while using substantial effort and withdrawing elsewhere. Visible productivity does not reveal the internal cost or rule out significant distress.'],['How long must symptoms last to be depression?','Diagnosis generally requires a qualifying symptom pattern for at least two weeks. Support can still be appropriate earlier or when fewer symptoms cause meaningful difficulty.'],['Can physical illness resemble depression?','Yes. Medical conditions and medicines can affect energy, sleep, concentration and mood. A clinician may recommend physical evaluation alongside a mental health assessment.']],
